Spec: SpecDD Color Settings Page

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Expose SpecDD highlighting keys through IntelliJ's standard editor color scheme UI.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.kt

Can read:
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/highlighting/SpecDDColorSettingsPageBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Implement IntelliJ `@ColorSettingsPage`.
  Return the SpecDD file type icon.
  Return a `@SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter`.
  Provide complete demo text that exercises every known SpecDD section and the major valid body forms.
  Include comments, explicit paths, globs, key-value lines, continuations, inline code spans, explicit symbols, all valid task markers, scenario steps, and repeated examples in the demo text.
  Expose descriptors for all SpecDD semantic highlighting keys.
  Provide default preview attributes for SpecDD-specific colors without using deprecated `@TextAttributesKey` registration overloads.
  Keep color scheme integration separate from tokenization.

Must not:
  Add plugin-specific settings or configuration UI.
  Report validation diagnostics.
  Define tokenization rules.
